L2 MAC Frame Parser
Topic: C++ · L2/MAC protocol parsing · Bit manipulation · Error handling


Phase 1 — Code Review  (~20 min)
Read the following buggy implementation. Find all bugs and quality issues before looking at the answers.

Code to review
// mac_parser.cpp
#include <cstdint>

enum class FrameType { MAC = 0, RLC = 1, PDCP = 2 };

struct L2Header {
    uint8_t  version;
    uint8_t  type;
    uint16_t length;
    uint32_t seq_num;
};

// Parses 7 bytes: [ver|type][len_hi][len_lo][seq3][seq2][seq1][seq0]
FrameType parse_header(const uint8_t* data, L2Header& header) {
    header.version = data[0] >> 4;
    header.type    = data[0] & 0xF;
    header.length  = (data[1] << 8) | data[2];
    header.seq_num = (data[3] << 24) | (data[4] << 16) |
                     (data[5] << 8)  |  data[6];
    return static_cast<FrameType>(header.type);
}


Try to find the bugs yourself first. There are 4 bugs and 3 quality issues.


Answers — Bugs Found
#
Type
Description
